WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.710
Since Keanu Reeves first hit Hollywood like
a cool breeze in the '80s, he's saved humanity

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:11.920
from robot slavery, kept a doomed bus from
exploding, and even made out with Paula Abdul.

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:12.920
"Whoa"

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:17.680
But even though Reeves is a pretty prolific
actor, he remains far more enigmatic than

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.580
many other celebrities… until now!

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:24.900
Here are some things you may not know about
Keanu Reeves.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:25.900
Bard brain

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:31.400
Thanks to his roles as dumb guy Ted in Bill
and Ted's Excellent Adventure and dumb guy

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:36.719
Tod in Parenthood, Reeves was in danger of
being typecast in the early '90s.

00:00:36.719 --> 00:00:38.649
"Now what?"

00:00:38.649 --> 00:00:42.710
That's why it was something of a surprise
when Kenneth Branagh cast Reeves as Don John

00:00:42.710 --> 00:00:48.409
in his 1993 screen adaptation of William Shakespeare's
Much Ado About Nothing.

00:00:48.409 --> 00:00:54.369
But Reeves had actually been performing Shakespeare
for years, dating back to a 1985 production

00:00:54.369 --> 00:00:57.640
of Romeo and Juliet at a Toronto theater school.

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:01.510
And My Own Private Idaho was based on Shakespeare’s
works.

00:01:01.510 --> 00:01:03.170
How much does he love Shakespeare?

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:08.159
He turned down a $12 million offer to star
in Speed 2 so that he could play Hamlet in

00:01:08.159 --> 00:01:10.740
a stage production in Manitoba, Canada.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.240
Now that's love...

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:18.289
"I had rather be a canker in a hedge than
a rose in his grace!"

00:01:18.289 --> 00:01:20.140
Haunted by...a jacket?

00:01:20.140 --> 00:01:25.750
While living in the New York area, young Reeves
encountered what can only be described as

00:01:25.750 --> 00:01:26.900
a ghost.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:29.219
A ghost jacket, anyway.

00:01:29.219 --> 00:01:33.780
There's really no explanation — so let's
just have Keanu tell the tale himself:

00:01:33.780 --> 00:01:34.850
"There's a doorway.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.979
All of the sudden we're looking over there
and this like jacket comes waving through

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:42.940
the doorway, like just an empty, there's no
head, there's no body, there's no legs, it's

00:01:42.940 --> 00:01:44.200
just there.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:45.600
And then it disappears.

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.179
And I was a little kid and I thought 'Ok well
that's interesting.'

00:01:48.179 --> 00:01:52.519
And then I looked over at the nanny, and she's
like this."

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:55.780
Whoa.

00:01:55.789 --> 00:01:57.250
He can’t quit smoking

00:01:57.250 --> 00:02:02.939
While smoking is often a youthful indiscretion,
Reeves was well into adulthood before he picked

00:02:02.939 --> 00:02:03.969
up the habit.

00:02:03.969 --> 00:02:09.940
He says he started doing it on the set of
the 1996 comedy Feeling Minnesota because

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:13.520
his character was a smoker, and then he just
got hooked.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:18.590
He's called smoking "a prison" that he'd love
to quit, but can't.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.769
Personal tragedies

00:02:20.769 --> 00:02:25.260
Reeves endured multiple heartbreaking tragedies
in rapid succession.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:31.400
He met actress and production assistant Jennifer
Syme in 1998, and the two fell in love.

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.940
In 1999, Syme and Reeves were expecting a
child together, but when Syme was almost full

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.260
term, doctors discovered the baby had passed
away.

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:45.500
The stress of the loss of the child contributed
to the demise of their relationship.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.629
Less than two years later, while driving home
from a party at Marilyn Manson's house in

00:02:49.629 --> 00:02:53.890
Los Angeles, Syme was killed in a single-car
accident.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.209
She was only 28 years old.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.069
Charity work

00:02:58.069 --> 00:03:03.379
Reeves is very close with his sister, Kim
Reeves, who was diagnosed with leukemia in

00:03:03.379 --> 00:03:04.480
the '90s.

00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:09.750
Filming on The Matrix Reloaded and The Matrix
Revolutions was reportedly delayed so Keanu

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:14.140
could spend more time with his sister and
help nurse her back to health.

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:20.010
In Kim's honor, Keanu has donated huge amounts
of his time and money to cancer charities,

00:03:20.010 --> 00:03:21.320
hospitals, and research facilities.

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:29.189
"I have a foundation that does some, it's
mostly directed towards healthcare."

00:03:29.189 --> 00:03:36.349
And he also works with organizations like
the SickKids Foundation and Stand Up to Cancer.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:38.189
Film crew favorite

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:43.319
While negotiating his contract for the two
Matrix sequels, Reeves scored a bunch of "back

00:03:43.319 --> 00:03:47.980
end" points, meaning he'd make a portion of
the movie's box office take in addition to

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.980
a salary.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:54.549
Instead of taking all the cash for himself,
Reeves diverted the money to the Matrix trilogy's

00:03:54.549 --> 00:04:00.230
costume and special effects teams, essentially
donating millions so the movies could be completed

00:04:00.230 --> 00:04:02.720
after the production nearly ran out of cash.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:09.090
He also bought each of the trilogy's 12 stuntmen
a Harley Davidson—his way of saying "thanks."

00:04:09.090 --> 00:04:10.430
Pay cuts

00:04:10.430 --> 00:04:15.299
If Reeves really wants to work with an actor
he admires, he isn't above foregoing a portion

00:04:15.299 --> 00:04:18.410
of his usual salary to help make it happen.

00:04:18.410 --> 00:04:22.880
He reportedly did exactly that so that he
could star in The Devil's Advocate with Al

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:26.450
Pacino and in The Replacements with Gene Hackman.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:28.420
"What's it gonna be Shane?"

00:04:28.420 --> 00:04:30.600
"I want the ball."

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:33.170
"Winners always do."

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.140
Motorcycle man

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:40.980
Reeves loves motorcycles so much that he started
his own business, the Arch Motorcycle Company,

00:04:40.980 --> 00:04:46.270
whose signature product is the Arch Motorcycle
KRGT-1.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:51.420
Designed and built with his friend and Arch
co-founder, bike architect Gard Hollinger,

00:04:51.420 --> 00:04:58.330
the custom built "superbikes" have two V-twin
engines and cost $78,000 each.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:04:59.790
Rad Keanu

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:05.390
Reeves has often been an inspiration for memes,
viral pictures, and the overall delight of

00:05:05.390 --> 00:05:06.600
the internet.

00:05:06.600 --> 00:05:12.220
Among the most famous: a viral video of Keanu
giving up his subway seat to someone who needed

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:13.220
it more.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:19.980
Then there's this uncanny 16th century painting
from the Uffizi Gallery in Florence, Italy,

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:24.220
which seems to suggest that Keanu is actually
a time traveler himself.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.540
And of course, there's the infamous Sad Keanu
meme.

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.630
Which actually made Keanu kind of… sad But
not that sad.

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:36.410
"I mean, do I wish that I didn't get my picture
taken while I was eating a sandwich on the

00:05:36.410 --> 00:05:37.850
streets of New York?

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:38.850
Ya."

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:41.380
Not quite the Wyld Stallyns

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:46.120
Shortly after the release of the Bill and
Ted movies, Reeves formed a garage band called

00:05:46.120 --> 00:05:48.650
Dogstar...in his actual garage.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:54.940
"I played in a band called Dogstar and we
made a couple of albums.

00:05:54.940 --> 00:05:56.750
I played electric bass."

00:05:56.750 --> 00:06:02.180
At their first gig, an up-and-coming band
called Weezer was their opening act, and Dogstar

00:06:02.180 --> 00:06:03.910
even played The Tonight Show.

00:06:03.910 --> 00:06:09.180
(Keanu Reeves slapping bass in his band Dogstar)

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:10.370
Thanks for watching!

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:14.460
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:18.770
And leave us a comment and let us know which
fact about Keanu Reeves surprised you the

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:19.270
most…

